     "confidence": 0.7,
     "rationale": "A u1 counter that rises within 99.6% of passes and wraps 4 times per pass. It increments at about 0.011 per second, with a median step of 3 between frames. The 63 resets in the window are mostly wraps of a 1-byte counter, so they do not indicate reboots. The weak sun correlation is probably a sampling artifact. [3/3 samples agree]"
    },
    {
     "offset": 17,
     "name": "battery_voltage_or_temperature_raw",
     "category": "power_battery",
     "unit": "mV",
     "scale": "raw * 1",
     "confidence": 0.2,
     "rationale": "A smooth, narrow-range u2 (p5-p95 of 761-808, spread 0.06) that rises strongly after sunrise (trend 0.84) with a long time constant (80 min or more). That fits a battery voltage or an internal temperature. The values are too low for a Li-ion cell in mV, so the unit and scale are uncertain, and the max of 48072 looks like a glitch or bad frame. It could also be a temperature in 0.1 degC or a similar scale. [2/3 samples agree]"
    }
   ],
   "health": "Not enough evidence for a firm verdict. The only reset-like signal is the 1-byte counter, which wraps by design, so reboots cannot be judged from it. The slow upward drift of offset 17 (about +2 raw units per 30 days) could be seasonal or a real trend, and its meaning is unclear."
